---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout pageId="contact">
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container page-hero__grid">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Contact</span><h1>Contact the society.</h1><p class="page-hero__lead">Use the form for membership questions, project proposals, collaborations, resource corrections, accessibility concerns, or media requests.</p></div>
    <div class="page-hero__side"><figure class="page-hero__figure"><img src="assets/images/photos/audio-jack.jpg" width="1200" height="960" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="An audio jack and its solder pads in close up"></figure><aside class="page-hero__aside"><strong>Instagram</strong><p><a class="text-link" data-instagram-link href="https://www.instagram.com/oberlin32engineering/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@oberlin32engineering ↗</a></p><strong>Direct inquiries</strong><p>Submit the form below and select the relevant topic.</p></aside></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container split">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">What to send</span>
      <h2>Choose the relevant topic.</h2>
      <ul class="check-list"><li>A question about joining or a planned event</li><li>A project problem, tool, space, or mentoring offer</li><li>An alumni, faculty, engineer, or researcher willing to speak</li><li>A campus organization interested in co-hosting something concrete</li><li>A correction to a resource or 3-2 link</li><li>An accessibility concern</li></ul>
      <div class="callout callout--warning"><p><strong>Academic questions:</strong> We can help you prepare questions and find official pages, but only authorized advisers and institutions can confirm requirements.</p></div>
    </div>
    <form class="form-shell" data-o32-form data-form-type="contact">
      <h2>Send a message</h2>
      <div class="form-grid">
        <label class="form-field"><span>Your name</span><input type="text" name="full_name" maxlength="120" autocomplete="name" required></label>
        <label class="form-field"><span>Email</span><input type="email" name="email" maxlength="254" autocomplete="email" autocapitalize="none" spellcheck="false" required></label>
        <label class="form-field form-field--full"><span>Topic</span><select name="topic"><option>General question</option><option>Membership</option><option>Project idea or support</option><option>Speaker or alumni conversation</option><option>Campus collaboration</option><option>Resource correction</option><option>Privacy or accessibility</option><option>Media request</option></select></label>
        <label class="form-field form-field--full"><span>Message</span><textarea name="message" maxlength="2500" required></textarea></label>
        <label class="honeypot" aria-hidden="true">Company<input type="text" name="company" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label>
        <div class="form-actions"><button class="button button--primary" type="submit">Send message</button><p class="form-status" data-form-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></div>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--soft">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Working with the society</span><h2>Propose one concrete next step.</h2></div><p>Include the audience, activity, timing, costs, access needs, and what you are asking students to do.</p></div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="card"><h3>Speakers and mentors</h3><p>Share a specific topic, your background, preferred format, available dates, and whether the conversation can be recorded or summarized.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Campus collaborators</h3><p>Suggest one event or project with a clear owner, timeline, room or equipment need, and division of responsibility.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Material support</h3><p>Describe the item, condition, safety information, restrictions, and whether the society would own, borrow, or dispose of it.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>
